WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.869 --> 00:00:05.189
For these marchers, Rosa Luxemburg and Karl
Liebknecht are real heroes.

00:00:05.189 --> 00:00:11.150
Thousands turned out to mark the 100th anniversary
of the deaths of the communist leaders.

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:18.910
Trudging 15 kilometres in the rain to the
couple's memorial.

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:22.740
Rosa Luxemburg and Karl Liebknecht were murdered
100 years ago.

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:24.390
Their struggle still counts.

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:26.890
We can see that in the rise of militarism.

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:31.130
The problems that we have have with racism
in Germany, the swing to the far right.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:34.670
Those are all reasons why we're here."

00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:37.410
No doubt, Rosa and Karl are their big idols.

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:42.059
These people here believe they must continue
the struggle the socialists and communists

00:00:42.059 --> 00:00:45.809
started 100 years ago.

00:00:45.809 --> 00:00:47.420
That's when tradition began.

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:52.629
More than 100,000 followers flanked the coffins
of the two revolutionary leaders.

00:00:52.629 --> 00:01:00.350
Luxemburg and Liebknecht were captured and
shot by right-wing paramilitaries.

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:05.910
Their deaths are still controversial today.

00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:10.040
Australian Tekle Setargew is studying physics
in Berlin.

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:18.230
He's active in leftwing student politics,
and an ardent admirer of Rosa Luxemburg.

00:01:18.230 --> 00:01:21.460
Rosa Luxemburg, she was important figure,
she was revolutionary.

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:23.650
She was also a very strong feminist.

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:31.240
She is one of the first women to find her
voice and make a powerful stand in the time

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:35.140
where even revolutionary discussions were
dominated by men.

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:38.660
The marchers make their way to Berlin's Central
Cemetery.

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:43.590
It's a place of pilgrimage for the Left in
what was once communist East Berlin.

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:48.100
Wreaths and carnations are laid.

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:52.990
Tekle finds it encouraging that these historical
figures remain so significant.

00:01:52.990 --> 00:02:04.200
For us, they represent our fight to improve
conditions for all workers around the world.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:09.509
And the society we are living in, we still
face the same conditions: workers, students,

00:02:09.509 --> 00:02:13.500
families, they are still exploited the same
way.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:20.860
We have to worry about our rents, having jobs
and becoming homeless and it has impacts all

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:22.740
over the world.

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:27.709
Across the way stands another memorial, this
one to the victims of communism.

00:02:27.709 --> 00:02:28.849
It's often ignored.

00:02:28.849 --> 00:02:34.670
But for this visitor it's important to lay
flowers HERE.

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:43.280
I think there's always a risk of the two of
them being romaticised.

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:48.890
It's important to remember the other side
of the story, that's if we want the whole

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:55.689
truth is to be told."

00:02:55.689 --> 00:03:00.080
Whether Karl Liebkecht and Rosa Luxemburg
were responsible for crimes committed later

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:01.840
in the name of communism is debatable.

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:06.680
But there's no doubt that the 100th anniversary
of their deaths is being used for political

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:08.370
purposes.

